dance</h3><p>Award practice credit for the correct result(s), with a valid method. Equivalent valid methods are accepted.</p><p>Marks are practice allocations; the source did not print a mark allocation for each question.</p>","sourceData":{"5":2,"6":3,"7":3,"8":4,"9":3,"10":1},"markingMode":"manual","typedAnswers":{"version":1,"fields":[{"label":"Mean (2 dp)","kind":"number","expected":"7.38","tolerance":0.005}],"fullQuestion":true,"scope":"All requested results."}},{"id":"maths-lower-data-910-data-interpretation-short-q4","subject":"Mathematics","area":"Mathematics","year":7,"originalYear":9,"examYear":0,"units":"Lower school","number":4,"sourceNumber":"4","sourceSection":"Short answer","source":"Data Interpretation · Short answer","section":"Calculator-assumed","types":["Calculator-assumed"],"calculatorMode":"assumed","responseTypes":["Short answer"],"marks":1,"marksOrigin":"Practice allocation; no printed question marks in source","topics":["Statistics and data"],"subtopics":["Statistical measures"],"mixed":false,"text":"Salaries: $28000, $17000, $21000, $36000, $21000, $41000, $53000 and $32000. Find the median salary of the eight employees.","hash":"746ed5efbbdc14e519bc3f4bee9f9d1b8ebcd6925753c5e818dbcd49eb318ee2","sourceFile":"Data Interpretation Test.docx","sourcePage":1,"sourceKeyFile":"Answers 9 10 Data.pdf","sourceKeyPage":6,"bankFile":"practice-studio-mathematics-data-interpretation-data910.json","addedAt":"2026-10-31T01:10:22Z","solutionOrigin":"supplied-key-checked-with-independent-calculation","scsa":{"curriculum":"Western Australian Curriculum Mathematics 2026","strand":"Probability and statistics","subStrand":"Probability and statistics","year":7,"foundation":true,"optional":false,"url":"https://k10outline.scsa.wa.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0004/1229467/Mathematics_Scope-and-sequence_7-10__For-implementation-in-2026.PDF"},"figures":0,"markingKeyPoints":[],"html":"<p>Salaries: $28000, $17000, $21000, $36000, $21000, $41000, $53000 and $32000.</p><p>Find the median salary of the eight employees.</p>","answerHtml":"<h3>Worked solution</h3><p>Ordered salaries: 17000,21000,21000,28000,32000,36000,41000,53000. Median = (28000 + 32000)/2 = $30000.</p><h3>Marking guidance</h3><p>Award practice credit for the correct result(s), with a valid method. Equivalent valid methods are accepted.</p><p>Marks are practice allocations; the source did not print a mark allocation for each question.</p>","sourceData":[28000,17000,21000,36000,21000,41000,53000,32000],"markingMode":"manual","typedAnswers":{"version":1,"fields":[{"label":"Median salary ($)","kind":"number","expected":"30000","tolerance":1e-09}],"fullQuestion":true,"scope":"All requested results."}},{"id":"maths-lower-data-910-data-interpretation-short-q5","subject":"Mathematics","area":"Mathematics","year":9,"originalYear":9,"examYear":0,"units":"Lower school","number":5,"sourceNumber":"5","sourceSection":"Short answer","source":"Data Interpretation · Short answer","section":"Calculator-assumed","types":["Calculator-assumed"],"calculatorMode":"assumed","responseTypes":["Short answer"],"marks":1,"marksOrigin":"Practice allocation; no printed question marks in source","topics":["Statistics and data"],"subtopics":["Histograms and frequency polygons"],"mixed":false,"text":"Draw a frequency histogram for the scores in the table.","hash":"881a7dc954e6ed51dbac9ce4937f356d71419d78b237b8dd642069cb373362fa","sourceFile":"Data Interpretation Test.docx","sourcePage":2,"sourceKeyFile":"Answers 9 10 Data.pdf","sourceKeyPage":7,"bankFile":"practice-studio-mathematics-data-interpretation-data910.json","addedAt":"2026-10-31T01:10:22Z","solutionOrigin":"supplied-key-checked-with-independent-calculation","scsa":{"curriculum":"Western Australian Curriculum Mathematics 2026","strand":"Probability and statistics","subStrand":"Probability and statistics","year":9,"foundation":false,"optional":false,"url":"https://k10outline.scsa.wa.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0004/1229467/Mathematics_Scope-and-sequence_7-10__For-implementation-in-2026.PDF"},"figures":0,"markingKeyPoints":[],"html":"<table><thead><tr><th>Score</th><th>Frequency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Draw a frequency histogram for the scores in the table.</p>","answerHtml":"<h3>Worked solution</h3><p>Draw touching columns centred on scores 1,2,3,4 with heights 4,2,4,6. Label the horizontal axis Score and vertical axis Frequency, with an appropriate uniform scale.</p><h3>Marking guidance</h3><p>Award practice credit for the correct results. Explanations, construction and drawn graphs require teacher review. Equivalent valid methods are accepted.</p><p>Marks are practice allocations; the source did not print a mark allocation for each question.</p>","sourceData":{"1":4,"2":2,"3":4,"4":6},"markingMode":"manual"},{"id":"maths-lower-data-910-data-interpretation-short-q6-stem","subject":"Mathematics","area":"Mathematics","year":7,"originalYear":9,"examYear":0,"units":"Lower school","number":6,"sourceNumber":"6 (stem-and-leaf plot, page 2)","sourceSection":"Short answer","source":"Data Interpretation · Short answer","section":"Calculator-assumed","types":["Calculator-assumed"],"calculatorMode":"assumed","responseTypes":["Short answer"],"marks":1,"marksOrigin":"Practice allocation; no printed question marks in source","topics":["Statistics and data"],"subtopics":["Stem-and-leaf plots"],"mixed":false,"text":"Distances in metres: 1.2, 1.3, 2.1, 3.1, 1.4, 4.1, 3.2, 2.2, 1.4, 3.2, 2.2, 3.3, 4.3, 2.3, 3.4, 1.5, 2.3, 4.4, 4.5, 3.4, 2.3, 3.4, 1.8, 2.4, 3.5, 2.5, 2.6, 1.9, 3.6, 2.9 Complete an ordered stem-and-leaf plot for the long-jump distances. Use whole metres as stems and tenths as leaves.","hash":"d8546e7f0b57017752d1c8dfba824350d5ead889f34cb932e2be175d1f1dfd81","sourceFile":"Data Interpretation Test.docx","sourcePage":2,"sourceKeyFile":"Answers 9 10 Data.pdf","sourceKeyPage